  "body": "<!--\r\n  Thanks for submitting a pull request!\r\n  Please provide enough information so that others can review your pull request.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR improves `insights` middleware to send events.\r\nThis PR also\r\n- exposes `sendEvent` to `connectRefinementList`\r\n- exposes `sendEvent` and `bindEvent` to `connectHits`\r\n- exposes `bindEvent` to `Hits` and its temlate\r\nto demonstrate how in practice it could work.\r\n\r\n[example](https://codesandbox.io/s/instantsearchjs-c9s30?file=/src/app.js) → It works when you check something in the `refinementList` and click any buttons in the `hits` and the custom hits widgets. (You can see the network panel of your browser to inspect the events sent to Algolia Insights)\r\n\r\n**Stacked PRs**\r\n1. [introduce `insights` middleware](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/pull/4446)\r\n2. [send events from hits and refinementList](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/pull/4456) ← current\r\n3. [implement sendEvent in all the connectors](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/pull/4463)\r\n4. [add tests](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/pull/4464)\r\n\r\n## Two cases\r\n\r\n1. The facet related connectors will run `sendEvent('click', ...)` along with `refine` and expose `sendEvent` to component layer.\r\n2. The hit related connectors will run `sendEvent('view', ...)` when rendering items and expose `sendEvent` to component layer. It will also expose `bindEvent` to templates which will be handled by insightsListener.\r\n\r\nWe expose `instantSearchInstance.sendEventToInsights()`:\r\n- which is called in connectors\r\n- which can be used by users when they manually want to send events\r\n\r\n## Details about the design\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>How to let users sendEvent from `hits` and `infiniteHits`?</summary>\r\n\r\n### `click` or `conversion` events from `connectHits`\r\n\r\nWe need to provide a way for users to send `click` or `conversion` events.\r\n\r\n#### Case 1. custom widget\r\n\r\nUsers can create custom components by using connectors:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nlet listener;\r\nconst renderFn = (renderOptions) => {\r\n  const { hits, sendEvent } = renderOptions;\r\n\r\n  const elem = /* ... */;\r\n  if (listener) {\r\n    elem.removeEventListener(\"click\", listener);\r\n  }\r\n  listener = (event) => {\r\n    const index = /* ... */;\r\n    const hit = hits[index];\r\n    sendEvent('conversion', hit, \"Product Bookmarked\");  // or 'click'\r\n    // ↑ I've got feedback from Mathieu that we cannot use default event names for 'click' and 'conversion' in the context of hits.\r\n    // It's because there can be many different types of clicks and conversions. Moreover the event names are used by Perso. So we should leave it to the users.\r\n  }\r\n  elem.addEventListener(\"click\", listener);\r\n};\r\nconst customWidget = connectHits(renderFn);\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd they can use `sendEvent` exposed by the connector. So this it looks okay in this case.\r\n\r\n#### Case 2. template\r\n\r\n`hits` and `infiniteHits` widgets are normally used with the `item` template.\r\n\r\n```js\r\ntemplates: {\r\n  item(hit) {\r\n    const html = /* ... */;\r\n    return html;\r\n  },\r\n},\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn this case, even if we expose `sendEvent` as in `item(hit, sendEvent, eventName)`, it's not easy to use because at this stage we don't have DOM element to attach event listeners.\r\n\r\nAnd even if we try to add event listeners outside the InstantSearch lifecycle,\r\n\r\n```js\r\nsearch.addWidgets([\r\n  hits({\r\n    container: \"#hits\",\r\n    templates: {\r\n      item(hit) {\r\n        /* ... */\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  }),\r\n]);\r\n\r\ndocument.querySelector(\"#hits\").addEventListener(\"click\", (event) => {\r\n  // How do we get `hit` object here?\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, in the end, we go back to what we've been doing:\r\n\r\n```js\r\ntemplates: {\r\n  item: (hit) => `\r\n    <button ${instantsearch.insights(\"clickedObjectIDsAfterSearch\", {\r\n      eventName: \"click-result\",\r\n      objectIDs: [hit.objectID],\r\n    })}>\r\n      Click event\r\n    </button>\r\n  `;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSimilarly,\r\n\r\n```js\r\ntemplates: {\r\n  item: (hit, bindEvent) => `\r\n    <button ${bindEvent(\"click\", hit, \"Product Bookmarked\")}>\r\n      Click event\r\n    </button>\r\n  `;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`bindEvent` is similar to `sendEvent`, but instead of delivering it to `insights` middleware, it returns a string like the following:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nreturn `data-insights-event=\"${btoa(JSON.stringify({ widgetType, eventType, aaMethod, payload ))}\"`\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd we can extend [insightsListener](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/master/src/lib/insights/listener.tsx#L26:L26) to handle this data- attribute.\r\n\r\nAccording to this addition, I'm in favor of deprecating the old way of\r\n\r\n```js\r\n    <button ${instantsearch.insights(\"clickedObjectIDsAfterSearch\", {\r\n      eventName: \"click-result\",\r\n      objectIDs: [hit.objectID],\r\n    })}>\r\n      Click event\r\n    </button>\r\n```\r\nand things related to it (for example, `withInsights` and `withInsightsListener`).\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Sending custom events</summary>\r\n\r\nIf users want to send raw custom event without any implication, they can call `search.sendEventToInsights(args)` and `args` will be sent to `insights` middleware if being used.\r\nThe minimum `args` for Algolia Insights is `{ aaMethod, payload }`. The full signature is `{ widgetType, eventType, aaMethod, payload }`.\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Default event names</summary>\r\n\r\n### Facet\r\nWe normally send only `click` event from these connectors: connectRefinementList, connectBreadcrumb, ...\r\nAnd its default event name is `Filter Applied`, which makes sense.\r\n\r\n### Hit\r\nHere we could have all of three types of events:\r\n- view\r\n- click\r\n- conversion\r\n\r\nIn case of `view`, we can safely use `Hits Viewed` as a default event name.\r\n\r\nHowever in case of `click` or `conversion`, we cannot force any default event name because there can be different types of events and if we use a default name for all, it can affect the quality of personalization. So we do not have any default name and let users decide.\r\n</details>",
